content.text:
The first page of `/v3/checkins` (cursor feed, no cursor = earliest page) returned:

```json
{"checkins": [
  {"id": "ci-001", "device_id": "dev-A"},
  {"id": "ci-002", "device_id": "dev-B"},
  {"id": "ci-003", "device_id": "dev-A"},
  {"id": "ci-004", "device_id": "dev-A"}
], "next_cursor": "cur_p1"}
```

The ids ascend (`ci-001` → `ci-004`), so the feed is ordered earliest-first; the first page holds the earliest check-ins. The very first row on the first page is `ci-001` with `device_id == "dev-A"` — that's dev-A's earliest check-in, found on the first page without needing to walk to `next_cursor` pages. I'll save it into a variable for the reconcile job.
